title: "triplet-proof: Monte Carlo framework for genetic code error-minimization"
abstract: >-
  Monte Carlo framework quantifying error-minimization in the standard genetic
  code (SGC) using two graph-theoretic metrics on the codon Hamming graph:
  Dirichlet energy and receiver noise distortion, scored against 8 PCA-derived
  amino acid physicochemical properties. A 2 x 2 factorial design crosses codon
  length (n = 2 vs n = 3) with alphabet size (10 vs 20 amino acids), scoring
  each condition against a degeneracy-preserving null of 1,000,000 random codes.
  The SGC lies beyond all 10^6 random codes on both metrics, and triplet
  architecture crosses an optimization threshold that doublet architecture does
  not, independently of alphabet size.
